# Cloudflare Pages response headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# Source of truth: deployment/cloudflare/_headers — the build copies this
# file verbatim to docs/_headers. GitHub Pages ignores it; it only takes
# effect if the site is ever deployed on Cloudflare Pages (which is
# prepared but NOT active — see docs-for-maintainers/cloudflare-pages.md).
#
# Deliberately conservative starting policy:
# - No Content-Security-Policy yet: the pages carry an inline pre-paint
#   theme script, and a CSP must be designed and tested against that
#   script, the local assets, external ETSI links, print and every
#   Playwright suite before it ships. 'unsafe-inline' merely to make a
#   CSP pass would weaken it to the point of theatre, so no CSP at all
#   until hashes/nonces are properly introduced and tested.
# - No one-year "immutable" caching: asset filenames are not fingerprinted
#   (style.css keeps its name across releases; only a ?v= query changes),
#   and immutable caching of an unhashed filename can pin visitors to
#   stale assets. Long-lived caching waits for fingerprinted filenames —
#   see docs-for-maintainers/cloudflare-pages.md.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
